# 杯叙 CupTale · HUSH

家庭私人调酒点单与配方管理系统（品牌 **HUSH**）。移动端优先网页；访客无登录点单；管理员开放进入 `/admin`。

## Stack

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion
- Prisma + Postgres (`DATABASE_URL`：Neon 或 Supabase)
- Images: Netlify → Supabase Storage (`cuptale-images` + `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`); optional Vercel Blob; local fallback `/public/uploads`
- DeepSeek OpenAI-compatible API (`base_url` + `deepseek-flash`) — **server-only**
- Zod for request validation; jose for admin session cookie（admin 门禁已开放）
- Deploy target may be **Netlify** (`@netlify/plugin-nextjs`) or Vercel

## Product boundaries (hard)

- **Guest never sees recipes**: ingredients, ml, steps, recipe notes must not appear in public pages or public API JSON.
- Drink public DTO may include: name, image, flavorText, taste tags (sweetness/acidity/strength/abv/glass/dairy/caffeine/allergens), availability flags.
- Admin lives under `/admin` with **no password** (open gate); do **not** link it from guest navigation.
- Guest public APIs must never return recipes; use `?admin=1` / `scope=admin` only for admin UI fetches.
- Drink (menu) and Recipe (private notebook) are separate; a drink may publish without a recipe.
- Recipe notebook flow: paste rough notes + photos → AI parse/chat（顺序与手法）→ save private recipe → later add photos → **上架为酒品**（copies taste tags + flavorText; guests still never see recipe internals）.
- Admin nav labels: **未上架** = recipes without a published drink; **已上架** = published drinks. List actions: 上架为酒品 / 下架 / 设为售罄.
- Order workflow: tap order → preview sheet (image + ingredient summary) → 开始制作 → `/admin/orders/[id]` shows private recipe and sets status `making` → 制作完毕 → `done` and back to orders.
- Netlify image upload needs Supabase Storage env; empty tables alone are not the upload failure cause（serverless 不能写本地 `public/uploads`）.
- Unavailable drinks: greyed out, not hidden; not orderable.
- Guest can track **only their own** orders via `publicToken` stored locally.

## UX / brand

- Brand name: **HUSH**; mark at `public/brand/hush-logo.jpg`（无副标题标语）.
- Mobile-first; guest IA: 首页 / 点单 / 我的; order page uses left category + right list.
- Visual: dark plum background (`#160C1F`), pink accent (`#FF6EC7`), soft lavender text; neon-bar calm, not dashboard clutter.
- Flow: home → order menu → drink detail → submit → my orders.
- Chinese UI copy: short and plain; avoid marketing fluff / “AI 文案感”.
- Quiet micro-interactions; pink glow sparingly on primary CTAs only.
- Local drink uploads go to `/public/uploads` (gitignored) — they do **not** appear on Netlify after git push. Production needs Supabase Storage or Vercel Blob.
- When opening local preview browsers: **only 2 windows** — guest `/` and admin `/admin/orders` (iPhone 16 Pro Max size).

## Code style

- Concise TypeScript; functional components; named exports.
- Prefer Server Components; mark `"use client"` only when needed.
- Directories/files: lowercase with dashes where practical.
- Descriptive names (`isAvailable`, `handleSubmit`); early returns; Zod at API edges.
- No secrets in client bundles or git; use env vars from `.env.example`.
- Preserve unrelated code; security-conscious on admin/recipe routes.
- When product rules or fixed prompts are decided in chat, append them to this rules file.
- **Production `prisma/schema.prisma` must stay `postgresql`** (mirror of `schema.postgres.prisma`). Local SQLite is only via `scripts/dev-local.mjs` / `schema.local.sqlite.prisma` — never commit SQLite as the main schema.

## DeepSeek flavor copy

- Call only from server (Route Handlers / server actions).
- Prompt must produce short literary flavor notes; **never reveal exact ingredients or ratios**.
- Support generate + regenerate; always allow human edit before save.

## DeepSeek recipe ingest (admin)

- `/api/ai/recipe` + `/api/ai/recipe/chat` parse hand notes into private recipe + suggested taste; always allow manual edit.
- Heuristic fallback must work without API key for basic `日期+酒名+原料ml` notes.

## Deploy notes

- Target Netlify (or Vercel); Framework Preset = Next.js.
- Required env: `DATABASE_URL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET`, `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`, Supabase keys for images.
- DB: Prisma Postgres (or Neon / Supabase). When connecting integration, Custom Prefix must be `DATABASE` so the var is `DATABASE_URL`.
- Keep `awesome-cursorrules-main/` local-only (gitignored) as a prompt library.
- Deploy fill-in checklist lives in `DEPLOY.md`.
